<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Electorate of Cologne</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Archbishopric of Cologne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> was the ecclesiastical principality of the archbishops of Cologne within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, one of its seven original electorates. Besides lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a> after the city of Cologne won its freedom, the archbishops ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-westphalia">Duchy of Westphalia</a> from 1180. The state lost its left-bank lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the 1790s and was dissolved in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/electorate-of-cologne.jpg" alt="Electorate of Cologne" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laurens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_St_George%27s_Cross.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
